<node id="AC Bridge">
  <data key="d0">AC Bridge</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of electrical bridge circuit used for measurement in Alternating Current systems, mentioned in the context of Chapter 3.&lt;SEP&gt;AC Bridge is an electrical circuit configuration used for measuring impedance, characterized by a null or balance condition where the detector current is zero.&lt;SEP&gt;An electrical circuit configuration used to measure unknown electrical impedances, depicted in Figure 3.7 and Figure 3.12.</data>
  <data key="d3">chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00029-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00031-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790516173</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chapter 3">
  <data key="d0">Chapter 3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific chapter within a document or book, identified as Chapter 3, which covers the topic of DC and AC Bridges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00000-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790508031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analog Signal">
  <data key="d0">Analog Signal</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of signal that varies continuously and are most signals in many systems, requiring processing for digital conversion.&lt;SEP&gt;The continuous input signal whose level determines the digital value in the counter.&lt;SEP&gt;A reference voltage level that the integrator output tracks; a state change in the comparator occurs when the integrator output matches this level.&lt;SEP&gt;Analog Signal represents a continuous signal in the Analog to Digital conversion system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00001-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00035-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00034-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00019-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790517902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A/D Converter">
  <data key="d0">A/D Converter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An Analog-to-Digital Converter, a device used to convert an analog signal into a digital format.&lt;SEP&gt;Analog-to-Digital Converter, a device that converts analog signals to digital data&lt;SEP&gt;A general device or circuit that converts an analog signal into a digital signal, specifically referenced in the context of integration with reset functions.&lt;SEP&gt;An Analog-to-Digital converter that operates using two voltage slopes.&lt;SEP&gt;An Analog-to-Digital converter, specifically described as a counter or ramp type, that processes input signals and provides digital output.&lt;SEP&gt;A/D Converter is a component in the Analog to Digital conversion system that converts the Sampled-Data Signal into a Digital Signal.&lt;SEP&gt;An Analog-to-Digital Converter utilizing a counter method where conversion time depends on the input signal size.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00001-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00033-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00041-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00023-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00019-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00026-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790518741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
