<node id="Circuit">
  <data key="d0">Circuit</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An electrical circuit configured with an input voltage Ein of 10 V and a fixed resistor Ra of 1KΩ, where the resistor Rb is selected from a set of 100kΩ resistors.&lt;SEP&gt;The electrical system described in Example 3.1, which is assumed to be in a null state with zero current through the galvanometer.&lt;SEP&gt;Circuit is the electrical network structure depicted in Figure 3.4, which consists of the voltage source E and resistors R1, R2, R3, R4, and Rg.&lt;SEP&gt;The electronic system connected according to the schematic in Fig.1, which is tested by varying analog inputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">Lab1::ch_00008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab4::ch_00003-chunk-000</data>
