<node id="Random Error">
  <data key="d0">Random Error</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An error in measurement that can be assigned a specific reason and avoided through precautions, often caused by impracticable noise and estimated by statistical analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00008-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790508811</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statistical Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Statistical Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method used to estimate random errors in measurements by increasing the frequency of measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;A method used to obtain quantitative information from data, including mean value, average deviation, and standard deviation, and to make judgments about variations or errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00018-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790513022</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A quantitative assessment of a parameter that is subject to random errors when noise is present and is subject to frequent repetition to allow for statistical estimation.&lt;SEP&gt;Measurement refers to the process or quantity being measured, as indicated in the chapter title.&lt;SEP&gt;Refers to the repeated set of observations of a specific variable, where the nth measurement is denoted as Xn and the average of these measurements is considered.&lt;SEP&gt;The act of quantifying a physical quantity, which is affected by multiple factors and may vary upon repetition.&lt;SEP&gt;Measurement is the process in which various types of errors, including random, gross, and systematic errors, can occur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00014-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00007-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790517985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
