<node id="Arithmetic Mean">
  <data key="d0">Arithmetic Mean</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The calculated average of the data values, computed as 49.9 in the example&lt;SEP&gt;Arithmetic Mean is a statistical measure representing the average value of a set of n numbers, denoted by x̄, calculated and defined by summing all numbers in the set and dividing by the count n.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00021-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00019-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790516208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deviation">
  <data key="d0">Deviation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The difference between each individual data value and the arithmetic mean&lt;SEP&gt;A metric calculated for each resistor, denoted as d_i, defined by the formula involving R_i and R_bar.&lt;SEP&gt;Deviation is a statistical metric defined as the difference between each individual piece of test data and the arithmetic mean of the dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;The difference between an individual resistor's resistance and the mean resistance, denoted as di.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00021-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab1::ch_00003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00019-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab1::ch_00005-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790518166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Algebraic Sum">
  <data key="d0">Algebraic Sum</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The sum of the deviations of each value</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00021-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790508812</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Average Deviation">
  <data key="d0">Average Deviation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The average magnitude of the deviations&lt;SEP&gt;A statistical measure of variation obtained through statistical analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Average Deviation, denoted as D, is a statistical measure calculated as the sum of absolute deviations divided by the number of values n.&lt;SEP&gt;The mean of the absolute deviations, calculated to be 0.3 (denoted as D).</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00021-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00018-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00020-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00022-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790518807</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Deviation">
  <data key="d0">Standard Deviation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A measure of the dispersion of the data values&lt;SEP&gt;Standard deviation is a statistical measure of dispersion calculated from the sample data, represented by the formula for square root of the sum of squared differences divided by sample size.&lt;SEP&gt;A statistical measure of data dispersion obtained through statistical analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Standard Deviation, denoted as S, is a statistical measure representing the degree to which values vary about the average value.&lt;SEP&gt;A statistical measure computed from a dataset, with a specific value of 0.294 derived in the input text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00021-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab1::ch_00004-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00018-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00020-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-1 Error in measurement::ch_00023-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790518459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
