<node id="Counter">
  <data key="d0">Counter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A component containing digital values that correspond to the level of the analog signal in the conversion process.&lt;SEP&gt;A digital component within the converter that tracks timing cycles to generate the digital output.&lt;SEP&gt;A component whose clock input is disabled by the comparator when the conversion condition is met, producing an output count proportional to the analog input voltage.&lt;SEP&gt;A digital component within the A/D converter that increments its count based on clock pulses to represent the magnitude of the analog input.&lt;SEP&gt;A digital component that overflows to generate a carry pulse which triggers control actions such as setting switch positions and can be frozen by external signals.&lt;SEP&gt;The counter receives pulses from the clock and counts them until it overflows at time t 2.&lt;SEP&gt;A digital component that generates a staircase ramp signal by counting clock pulses for analog-to-digital conversion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00035-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00036-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00025-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00033-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00038-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00037-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00026-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790518741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
