<node id="Capacitance">
  <data key="d0">Capacitance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A component parameter that, along with resistance, affects the integrator output when varying with temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property of an electrical component representing its ability to store energy in an electric field, used as the standard for measurements in Maxwell bridges.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical quantity that is measured using ac bridges.&lt;SEP&gt;A circuit parameter represented by C in the text, which appears in the impedance arms and balance equation formulas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00035-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00035-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00027-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00036-chunk-000</data>
