<node id="R1">
  <data key="d0">R1</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">R1 is a designator for a resistance component that appears across various electrical circuit configurations, with its specific function and value determined by the context of the schematic. In precision measurement circuits, R1 often serves as a known reference resistor. It is documented in a Wheatstone Bridge circuit with a resistance value of 15 Ohms and in a Kelvin Bridge circuit with a specified value of 5 Ohms. In specific documentation, such as Figure 3.4, R1 is identified as a fixed resistor with a resistance value of 1 kΩ (1000 ohms) in a DC bridge circuit.

Beyond fixed-value resistors, R1 denotes functional positions within more complex networks. In general resistor networks, it represents the first resistor in the sequence. Within the Murray Loop configuration, R1 is identified as a specific component or segment integral to the loop's structure. Furthermore, in other bridge circuit applications, R1 acts as a resistance element that, together with R3, establishes the required balance ratio for components Ra and Rb. Due to the diverse application of the label R1 in electronic engineering, its physical characteristics range from low-Ohm values for precision sensing to kilo-Ohm values for general bridging, necessitating context-specific identification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00023-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00015-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00024-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00022-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab2::ch_00000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00025-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790518184</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="R2">
  <data key="d0">R2</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A resistance component in the Kelvin Bridge circuit related to R1 by the equation R1 = 0.5 R2.&lt;SEP&gt;R2 denotes the second resistor in the resistor network&lt;SEP&gt;R2 is a known reference resistor with a resistance value of 0.5 times R1.&lt;SEP&gt;R2 is a resistor in Figure 3.4 with a resistance value of 1.6kΩ.&lt;SEP&gt;A known resistance component in the Wheatstone Bridge circuit, assigned a value of 40 Ohms.&lt;SEP&gt;A variable resistor in the DC bridge circuit with a maximum value of 100 KΩ.&lt;SEP&gt;A component or segment labeled R2, part of the Murray Loop configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00023-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00015-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00024-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab2::ch_00000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00025-chunk-000</data>
