  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">An unknown resistance value in the Kelvin Bridge circuit that is to be calculated.&lt;SEP&gt;Rx represents a resistance variable in the circuit equations, later calculated to be related to the value 4.941.&lt;SEP&gt;Rx is the unknown resistance value calculated as 0.01 ohms using the ratio of two known reference resistors.&lt;SEP&gt;The unknown resistor whose value needs to be determined in the circuit described in Example 3.1.&lt;SEP&gt;A circuit component, likely a resistor, whose value is to be calculated in Example 3.2.&lt;SEP&gt;The unknown resistance component in the Wheatstone Bridge circuit, which is calculated to be 18.75 Ohms based on the balance condition.&lt;SEP&gt;An unknown resistance in the DC bridge circuit, selectable up to 100 KΩ, with an example value of 50 KΩ.</data>
