<node id="Balance Condition">
  <data key="d0">Balance Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Balance Condition, also known as null condition, is the state in an AC bridge where the current through the detector is zero, indicating no voltage difference across the detector.&lt;SEP&gt;The specific state of the bridge where the voltage drops are equal and no current flows through the galvanometer, characterized by the ratio equation R2/R1 = R4/R3.&lt;SEP&gt;The state of equilibrium in the Wheatstone Bridge circuit that is detected by the galvanometer acting as a null detector.&lt;SEP&gt;The principle in a Wheatstone Bridge where the ratio of resistances in opposite arms results in a zero current flow, allowing for the calculation of an unknown resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;The state of the Wheatstone Bridge where the current through the null detector is zero and the voltage across resistor R3 equals the voltage drop across resistor R4.&lt;SEP&gt;The specific state in a bridge circuit where the differential voltage is zero, allowing for precise resistance and impedance measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00029-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00004-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab2::ch_00000-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790516191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Detector">
  <data key="d0">Detector</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Detector is a component in the AC bridge circuit that measures current; under balance condition, the current through it becomes zero.&lt;SEP&gt;A component included in the AC bridge circuit shown in Figure 3.12, used for detecting balance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00029-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chap 3 DC&amp;AC BRIDGES::ch_00031-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790516173</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 3.10">
  <data key="d0">Figure 3.10</data>
