<node id="Resistor">
  <data key="d0">Resistor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Resistor is a physical electronic component whose resistance value is measured and analyzed in the provided sample data to calculate statistical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental electrical component, typically denoted by R, that is part of the time constant RC in the integrator circuit.&lt;SEP&gt;A two-terminal electronic component that the voltage is measured across in the example problem.&lt;SEP&gt;A passive electronic component used in the R-2R Ladder DAC circuit; the design requires only values of R and 2R.&lt;SEP&gt;A general electrical component in the Wheatstone Bridge circuit that is varied to achieve a balance condition where the null detector current is zero.&lt;SEP&gt;Electronic components with specific resistance values, identified by indices 1 through 20 in the dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;A passive electronic component that limits the flow of electric current, with specific resistance values (R and R + Δ) defined in the bridge circuit.</data>
