  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The general technology for converting digital signals to analog signals, specifically referenced by its resolution limits such as 8-bit and 12-bit.&lt;SEP&gt;A DAC is a data converter whose output accuracy is described by full-scale error. In the example text, the DAC has a full-scale output of 9.375 V and an accuracy of ± 0.01% F.S.</data>
  <data key="d3">chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chapter 5  ADC and DAC::ch_00004-chunk-000</data>
