<node id="Insertion Error">
  <data key="d0">Insertion Error</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A calculated percentage metric used to quantify the deviation between the true and measured output voltage of an electronic circuit involving a 100kΩ resistor.&lt;SEP&gt;The measurement inaccuracy introduced when a meter is connected into a circuit for testing, which is the subject of the inquiry.&lt;SEP&gt;Insertion error is a measurement error discussed in the table of resistor measurements, defined as the deviation between the true and measured electromotive force values due to the insertion of a measuring instrument into a circuit.&lt;SEP&gt;Insertion Error is a specific type of error likely examined in the context of Part B, involving the erroneous insertion of data or elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">Lab1::ch_00009-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab1::ch_00011-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab1::ch_00010-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Lab1::ch_00007-chunk-000</data>
