  <data key="d0">Shannons Sampling Theorem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A fundamental principle in signal processing stating that a signal can be perfectly reproduced from its samples if the sampling interval is no greater than half the signal's maximum frequency (1/2 f_max).</data>
